---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { capabilityState } from "../../utilities/public-capabilities";

const explorer = capabilityState("explorer");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Damp & Mould"
  description="A bounded explanatory case showing how Enterprise Reality can support a Damp & Mould investigation across fragmented records and evidence."
  canonicalPath="/case-studies/damp-and-mould/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section">
    <div class="container page-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Canonical case</p>
        <h1>Damp &amp; Mould is a real-world problem pattern</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A resident reports persistent damp and mould. The enterprise must
          understand the situation across people, property, observations,
          decisions and history before it can responsibly consider what follows.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="identities">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Persistent identities</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="identities">The situation is not one record</h2>
        <p>
          The resident, property, tenancy, building, inspection, repair and
          responsible roles persist even when different systems describe them in
          different ways.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="proposition">One real situation. Many related aspects.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="landscape">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Illustrative system landscape</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="landscape">Observations are distributed</h2>
        <p>
          A housing example may distribute a resident report, tenancy record,
          inspection notes, photographs, moisture readings, repair history and
          follow-up record across separate systems. This is illustrative, not a
          claim about a particular housing provider or deployment.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="relationship relationship--observations"
        aria-label="Illustrative related aspects of the situation"
      >
        <li>Resident and tenancy</li><li>Property and inspection</li><li>
          Repair and follow-up
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="questions">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Fragmentation</p>
      <h2 id="questions">Cross-boundary questions emerge</h2>
      <p>
        Do the records concern the same property and resident? What was
        observed, by whom, and when? Which repair or inspection relates to which
        report? What is known, what conflicts, and what remains missing?
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reconnection">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reconstruction</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="reconnection">
          Re-establish identity and reconnect relationships
        </h2>
        <p>
          Enterprise Reality connects representations to persistent identities,
          then restores relationships among the resident, property, tenancy,
          inspection, repair and accountable roles.
        </p>
        <h3>Events and history</h3>
        <p>
          A chronology can reconnect a report, inspection, repair authorisation,
          contractor activity and follow-up without treating a current system
          field as the whole history.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="sequence sequence--horizontal"
        style="--sequence-count: 4"
        aria-label="Illustrative progression"
      >
        <li>Reported</li><li>Inspected</li><li>Repaired</li><li>
          Observed again
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="evidence">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why the account is believed</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="evidence">
          Evidence, provenance and uncertainty remain visible
        </h2>
        <p>
          Each observation needs its source and context. An inspection finding,
          resident account, photograph or repair record may support, contradict
          or leave a question unresolved. Disagreement and incomplete evidence
          are preserved rather than hidden.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="sequence" aria-label="Evidence relationship">
        <li>Observation</li><li>Evidence and provenance</li><li>
          What is currently justified
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="coherent-reality">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coherent Enterprise Reality</p>
      <h2 id="coherent-reality">Establish what can currently be understood</h2>
      <p>
        The result is a governed account of the situation and its limits: not a
        replacement housing system, and not an assertion that every question is
        settled.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/platform/"
          >See how the Platform makes this governed understanding executable</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="explorer">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Investigation</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="explorer">Explorer provides the investigation experience</h2>
        <p>
          Explorer can help people navigate the identities, relationships,
          evidence and chronology that form the investigation. It is an
          authorised product with implemented and demonstrated programme
          capability; public commercial availability is not claimed.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/explorer/">Understand the Explorer experience</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="authority-note">
        Programme standing: {explorer.programmeStanding}. Capability maturity: {
          explorer.maturity
        }.
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reasoning">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">After understanding</p>
      <h2 id="reasoning">Evidence-bound reasoning and possible action</h2>
      <p>
        Governed reasoning may assess relationships, evidence and policy to
        explain what is supported, not supported or indeterminate. A resulting
        action proposal may support accountable consideration, but it is not
        automatic execution or autonomous remediation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="ai-boundary">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI boundary</p>
      <h2 id="ai-boundary">AI remains advisory</h2>
      <p>
        AI may assist retrieval, explanation or navigation. It does not
        establish truth, resolve evidence by itself, approve action or operate a
        production housing service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="case-boundary">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">What this case demonstrates</p>
      <h2 id="case-boundary">A bounded investigation pattern</h2>
      <p>
        This case demonstrates how a Damp &amp; Mould investigation pattern can
        be understood through Enterprise Reality. It is not a customer story,
        production-housing claim, operational automation claim or commercial
        availability statement.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style></style>
